## File-Type-Specific Agent Behavior

### Code Files vs Text Files

| Aspect | Code Files (*.ts, *.py, *.java) | Text Files (*.txt, *.md) |
|--------|--------------------------------|--------------------------|
| **Agent approach** | Syntax-aware edits | Plain text edits |
| **Format preservation** | High (indents, braces) | Medium (spacing only) |
| **Import analysis** | Tracks imports/exports | N/A |
| **Error detection** | May check for syntax errors | N/A |
| **Test generation** | May suggest unit tests | N/A |

### Binary and Generated Files

The agent automatically skips these file types:

| Category | Patterns | Reason |
|----------|----------|--------|
| **Binary files** | `*.bin`, `*.exe`, `*.dll`, `*.o`, `*.class` | Cannot be meaningfully edited as text |
| **Minified files** | `*.min.js`, `*.min.css` | Not human-readable |
| **Build artifacts** | `dist/`, `build/`, `node_modules/` | Auto-excluded by convention |
| **Generated code** | `*.gen.ts`, `*.pb.go` | Generated, not meant for manual edit |
| **Compiled files** | `*.pyc`, `*.class`, `*.pyo` | Source is the editable version |
| **Binary data** | `*.png`, `*.jpg`, `*.pdf` (text) | Corrupted when opened as text |

### Skip Patterns Configuration

```json
{
  // Files agent will not read or search
  "files.exclude": {
    "**/.git": true,
    "**/node_modules": true,
    "**/dist": true,
    "**/build": true,
    "**/*.min.*": true,
    "**/*.gen.*": true,
    "**/vendor": true,
    "**/third_party": true
  },
  
  // Files agent will not search by default
  "search.exclude": {
    "**/node_modules": true,
    "**/dist": true,
    "**/build": true,
    "**/*.log": true,
    "**/.DS_Store": true
  }
}
```

