## Custom File Associations

### Mapping Extensions to Language IDs

You can configure how Cursor interprets specific file types:

```json
{
  // Custom file associations
  "files.associations": {
    "*.config": "jsonc",
    "*.tsconfig": "jsonc",
    "*.custom": "typescript",
    "*.vue": "vue",
    "*.svelte": "svelte",
    "*.graphql": "graphql",
    "*.proto": "proto"
  },
  
  // Agent-specific file type mapping
  "cursor.agent.fileTypes": {
    "*.spec.ts": "test",
    "*.test.ts": "test",
    "*.config.js": "config",
    "*.env": "plaintext",
    "*.yml": "yaml",
    "*.yaml": "yaml"
  }
}
```

### Agent-Aware File Types

Custom file types can influence agent behavior:

```json
{
  "cursor.agent.fileTypeBehavior": {
    // Test files get different treatment
    "test": {
      "toolPreference": "Write",
      "autoGenerate": true,
      "skipOnEdit": false
    },
    
    // Config files are validated
    "config": {
      "toolPreference": "Write",
      "validateOnWrite": true,
      "autoFormat": true
    },
    
    // Template files get special handling
    "template": {
      "toolPreference": "Write",
      "preservePlaceholders": true
    }
  }
}
```

