## File-Type-Based Rule Loading

### How File Types Trigger Rules

Rules with `globs` patterns are loaded when matching files are in context:

```markdown
<!-- .cursor/rules/typescript-rules.mdc -->
---
description: "TypeScript-specific coding standards"
globs: ["*.ts", "*.tsx", "*.mts"]
tags: [typescript, ts, tsx]
---

# TypeScript Rules
<!-- Agent sees these rules when working with .ts files -->
```

```markdown
<!-- .cursor/rules/python-rules.mdc -->
---
description: "Python-specific coding standards"
globs: ["*.py", "*.pyi"]
tags: [python, py]
---

# Python Rules
<!-- Agent sees these rules when working with .py files -->
```

### Rule Matching by File Type

| File Pattern | Rules Loaded |
|-------------|-------------|
| `*.ts`, `*.tsx` | TypeScript rules, general rules |
| `*.py` | Python rules, general rules |
| `*.md` | Markdown rules, documentation rules |
| `*.json` | JSON validation rules |
| `*.yaml`, `*.yml` | YAML rules |
| `*.ipynb` | Notebook rules, Python rules |
| `*.sql` | SQL rules |
| `*.html`, `*.css` | Web rules |

